# Project standing orders

Read [docs/constitution.md](../../docs/constitution.md) at least once in every context window. If it is still a TEMPLATE, write the project vision with the user before other work.

Also read:

1. [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md)

Non-trivial changes need an Agent Note under `.agents/notes/{lifecycle}/{class}/`.

Before automated research, classify the work as a spike, an experiment, or a campaign. Follow [lab/AGENTS.md](../../lab/AGENTS.md) for lab work. Campaign toolkit: [.agents/skills/README.md](../../.agents/skills/README.md).

Experiments: predictions are committed in `lab/experiments/planned/` before any run. Never add `## Results` there. Follow [lab/experiments/AGENTS.md](../../lab/experiments/AGENTS.md) and `.agents/skills/run-experiment/SKILL.md`.

After note or experiment edits, run `python scripts/verify_template.py` and report the result. Failures are errors, not hints.
